# Conventional Commits

Every git commit message MUST follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

Format:

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

Rules:

- `type` is required. Prefer: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`
- Description is required: imperative, lowercase start, no trailing period, concise
- `feat` = a new user-facing capability; `fix` = a bug fix
- Append `!` after type/scope for a breaking change (e.g. `feat(api)!: remove unversioned routes`)
- Breaking changes MUST also include a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer explaining what changed and what callers must do
- Footers use `Token: value` or `Token #value` (e.g. `Fixes #123`)
- Do not use `--no-verify` or skip hooks to bypass this format

Examples:

```
feat(claims): return claim age in days on get-by-ucr

fix(api): reject requests missing X-Api-Key

docs: document demo API key in README

feat(auth)!: require API key on all /api routes

BREAKING CHANGE: unauthenticated calls now return 401
```
